From 63106e20e4a620f2be4b39f00e64db1bd0193247 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 11:26:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pkg/lps: gitignore the bundled VyOS qcow2 so linuxkit doesn't
 tag dirty

The 750MB VyOS image lives at pkg/lps/images/small-vyos-ssh-nat.qcow2
in the working tree but isn't tracked in git. Without this entry,
linuxkit's pkg hash calculator sees the untracked file and computes
'<sha>-dirty-<short>' as the LPS image tag, which then can't be pulled
from docker.io at rootfs-assembly time and breaks the build.

Signed-off-by: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
---
 pkg/lps/.gitignore | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 pkg/lps/.gitignore

diff --git a/pkg/lps/.gitignore b/pkg/lps/.gitignore
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..51f889ba1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pkg/lps/.gitignore
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# VyOS qcow2 image is large (~750MB) and lives outside git tracking.
+# Without this entry, the untracked file makes linuxkit compute a
+# "-dirty-…" tag for the LPS pkg, which then can't be pulled at rootfs
+# assembly time and fails the build.
+images/*.qcow2
-- 
2.51.0

